# ADR-0001 Addendum A — human review gate on content-sensitive paths.
#
# What this file does and does NOT do:
#   - It REQUESTS review from the owners below on every PR touching these paths.
#   - It only BLOCKS merge if `main` branch protection sets
#     `require_code_owner_reviews: true`. It currently does not (see WIC-1064): the
#     enforcement of record in this repo is the REQUIRED STATUS CHECKS
#     ("Lint & Test", "Secrets-access content policy"), which cannot be satisfied by
#     a human decision. CODEOWNERS here is the advisory backstop for phrasings the
#     Layer 2 pattern set misses.
#
# tools/secrets-access-lint/ is listed deliberately: the linter self-excludes that
# directory (hard-coded, not a user-editable ignore file), so content placed inside it
# is not scanned by Layer 2. Review on that path is the compensating control.

.github/workflows/content-policy.yml   @alwick
.github/CODEOWNERS                     @alwick
tools/secrets-access-lint/             @alwick
.gitleaks.toml                         @alwick
CLAUDE.md                              @alwick
docs/architecture/                     @alwick
